        "original_id": "8cf3f12f-e58e-5c14-ab26-7f48bb6e8443",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Augusta Canal, Savannah River, Augusta, New Orleans\n- Structures: New Orleans Outfall Canals, levees, floodwalls, Butt Memorial Bridge\n- Roads: 15th Street\n\nFacts:\n- The Augusta Canal is fed by the Savannah River.\n- The Augusta Canal passes through three levels over approximately 13 miles in suburban and urban Augusta before its water returns to the river at various locations.\n- The New Orleans Outfall Canals have 13 miles of levees and floodwalls lining their sides.\n- The Butt Memorial Bridge is a road bridge in Augusta, Georgia, that carries 15th Street over the Augusta Canal.",
